---
description: Challenge one actual meaning against source scope and candidate lineage.
args:
  reading: MeaningReading
  source: CorpusSource
  graph: EvidenceGraph
  grammar: GrammarReport
returns: ReadingChallenge
---
1. Capture this actual reading and its actual retained survivor/attempt lineage in a typed scoped NL ReadingChallenge literal. Exclude ideal held-out answers and repaired-note wording.
2. Verify the reading's marker/boundary choices correspond to its actual hypothesis rather than another survivor's attractive interpretation. Trace exact original surface spans and real returned role/context contributions.
3. Challenge any scene-truth substitution, topic/agent conflation or new prospective claim unsupported by the supplied candidate/context. Distinguish a wrong inference from a genuine unresolved reference.
4. Preserve source-excluded elicitation fields: a candidate not tested about future expectation is not automatically contradicted by silence. Conversely an actual decided target difference cannot disappear in free translation prose.
5. A context-defined referent can resolve an actual grammatical alternative only under a source-authorized contextual rule. A clear depicted actor does not override a incompatible marker prediction.
6. Return grounded only when the actual source/prediction chain supports the reading; contradicted for a grounded incompatible claim; unresolved for missing lineage/meaning. Cite actual original witnesses for decided findings.
7. Parent retains the challenge without modifying the reading or grammar history; semantic repair belongs to a separately authorized revision, not this audit.
